"]},{"seq":13,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:33:37.033448875Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -10"]},{"seq":14,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:33:59.061762875Z","text":"Good, compiles with 1 sorry. Now let me work on the boundedness proof. The key steps:\n\n1. Every `z ∈ ℂ` can be written as `z = z₀ + n + mI` where `z₀ ∈ [0,1) + [0,1)I` (fundamental domain)\n2. `f(z) = f(z₀)` by repeated application of periodicity\n3. `range f ⊆ f '' (fundamental domain)` (actually equality, but ⊆ suffices)\n4. `f '' (compact set)` is compact (continuous image of compact) hence bounded\n\nFor step 1, I need `Int.floor` for the decomposition. For step 2, I need to show `f(z + n) = f(z)` for integer `n` (by induction on the periodicity).\n\nLet me think about the cleanest approach. The periods are `1` and `I`. For any `z`, write `z = (Re z - Int.floor (Re z)) + (Im z - Int.floor (Im z)) * I + Int.floor (Re z) + Int.floor (Im z) * I`.\n\nThe fractional parts give `z₀ ∈ [0,1) + [0,1)I ⊆ [0,1] + [0,1]I`. The integer parts give the lattice translate.\n\nFor the periodicity, I need: `f(z + ↑n) = f(z)` for all `n : ℤ`, and `f(z + ↑m * I) = f(z)` for all `m : ℤ`. This follows from the base case `f(z + 1) = f(z)` (or `f(z + I) = f(z)`) by induction.\n\nLet me write the periodicity lemma and the boundedness proof:"},{"seq":15,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:33:59.062271306Z","tools":["write_file"],"previews":["write_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":16,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:10.642382864Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -30"]},{"seq":17,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:21.446831190Z","text":"Several issues. Let me fix the `Int.induction_on` cases names and the `IsBounded.subset` argument order. Let me also simplify the structure:"},{"seq":18,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:21.447549839Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":19,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:33.861777186Z","text":"Now fix the main proof. The `IsBounded.subset` takes the set as explicit arg. Let me restructure:"},{"seq":20,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:33.862256327Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":21,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:42.570322151Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -25"]},{"seq":22,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:52.448621478Z","text":"The `Int.induction_on` uses `zero`, `succ`, `pred` not `base`, `step`, `neg_step`. And `IsBounded.mono` doesn't take `s` as a named arg. Let me fix both:"},{"seq":23,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:52.449321272Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":24,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:58.329238190Z","text":"Now fix the `IsBounded.mono`:"},{"seq":25,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:34:58.338702800Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && grep -rn \"def IsBounded.mono\\|theorem IsBounded.mono\\|lemma IsBounded.mono\\|theorem.*mono."]},{"seq":26,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:35:02.835869029Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && grep -rn \"theorem.*mono\\|lemma.*mono\" .lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/"]},{"seq":27,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:35:10.997477358Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && grep -rn \"IsBounded.*subset\\|theorem.*subset.*IsBounded\\|IsBounded.mono\" .lake/packages/ma"]},{"seq":28,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:35:21.356050840Z","te