ct that any integer is a difference of naturals.\n\nActually, let me try `norm_num` or `ring_nf` with explicit casts:"},{"seq":37,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:36:06.054766920Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":38,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:36:15.328673352Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -20"]},{"seq":39,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:36:28.007065175Z","text":"The `norm_num` for `↑(↑k + 1) : ℂ` fails because `↑k + 1` is `Nat + Nat` which can't be cast to ℂ directly. The issue is `Int.induction_on` with `succ` gives `n = ↑k + 1` where the `+1` is on `ℤ` not `ℕ`. Let me check: `Int.induction_on` with `| succ k hk |` has `n = ↑k + 1` where `k : ℕ` and `↑k : ℤ`, so `↑k + 1 : ℤ`. Then `↑(↑k + 1) : ℂ` coerces the Int to ℂ. The issue is `norm_num` can't handle this.\n\nLet me just use `Int.cast_add` explicitly:"},{"seq":40,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:36:28.007606173Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":41,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:36:36.810591758Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -20"]},{"seq":42,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:36:36.952445013Z","text":"[auto-continue 1/8]"},{"seq":43,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:36:47.117229069Z","text":"The `Int.cast_add` pattern `↑(?m + ?n)` doesn't match `↑(↑k + 1)` because `↑k + 1` is already `Int + Int` but the cast is from `ℤ → ℂ` and the pattern expects a different form. Let me try `show` instead of `rw`:"},{"seq":44,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:36:47.117660998Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":45,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:36:47.117711642Z",