mit, then try to close the sorry:"},{"seq":80,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:03.191892361Z","tools":["write_file"],"previews":["write_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/status.json"]},{"seq":81,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:08.776686437Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && git add problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean problems/a93J05/status.json && git commit -m \"a93J0"]},{"seq":82,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:08.912799180Z","text":"[auto-continue 2/8]"},{"seq":83,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:21.056636757Z","text":"Let me try to close the final sorry. The key: show `f(z) = f(φ(fract z.re, fract z.im))` by applying periodicity, then show membership in the image."},{"seq":84,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:21.057229463Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":85,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:29.784526457Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -25"]},{"seq":86,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:40.569727802Z","text":"Three issues:\n1. The `h1` approach is wrong — let me remove it entirely.\n2. `periodic_int_aux 1` gives `f(w + n * 1)` not `f(w + n)`. Need `n * 1 = n`.\n3. `ext` on ℂ needs a different approach.\n\nLet me fix all three:"},{"seq":87,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:40.570417703Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":88,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:50.031796142Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -20"]},{"seq":89,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:57.841709711Z","text":"The `Complex.ext` is solving goals too eagerly (the `simp` closes both goals). And `hz_eq` doesn't get used because `rw [← hz_eq]` fails to find the pattern. The issue: `hz_eq : z = w + ...` but the goal is about `f z`, and `rw [← hz_eq]` would need `z` to appear. But `z` DOES appear in `f z`. The issue is the pattern `w + ↑⌊z.re⌋ + ↑⌊z.im⌋ * I` doesn't match because `z` is in the goal, not the expanded form.\n\nWait — `rw [← hz_eq]` rewrites `w + floor_re + floor_im*I` to `z`. But the goal `f z ∈ ...` doesn't have `w + ...`. I should rewrite the OTHER way: `rw [hz_eq]` to replace `z` with `w + ...`:\n\nActually no — I need `f z` to become `f (w + floor_re + floor_im*I)`. So `rw [hz_eq]` at the goal would replace `z` with `w + ...`. But the goal is `f z ∈ ...` and `hz_eq : z = w + ...`. Let me use `rw [hz_eq]`:"},{"seq":90,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:40:57.842424620Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":91,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:03.566878723Z","text":"Also fix the `hz_eq` proof — the `Complex.ext` with `simp` closes both goals at once, but then the second `·` has no goals. Let me restructure:"},{"seq":92,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:03.567520716Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":93,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:12.718592913Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -25"]},{"seq":94,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:17.749060802Z","text":"The `simp` in the `hz_eq` proof closes the goal before `ring` runs (the `w` unfolds via `simp`). And the membership proof has wrong argument order. Let me fix both:"},{"seq":95,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:17.749528610Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":96,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:22.084933855Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":97,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:31.507564383Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -25"]},{"seq":98,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:38.547054600Z","text":"The `simp` is solving the goal before `ring` runs. And the membership has wrong arg order. Let me fix: the `simp` reduces the goal to something `ring` can't handle (or it closes it). Let me use `show` + `ring` instead:"},{"seq":99,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:38.547667436Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":100,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:48.536879406Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -20"]},{"seq":101,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:54.244128580Z","text":"The `show` doesn't match because of how `Complex.re` distributes. Let me try `simp only` with the right lemmas, then `omega`:"},{"seq":102,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:54.244842420Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":103,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:59.630470661Z","text":"Also fix the membership proof — `Set.mem_Icc` gives `a ≤ x ∧ x ≤ b`, so I need `⟨0 ≤ s, s ≤ 1, 0 ≤ t, t ≤ 1⟩`:"},{"seq":104,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:41:59.631124805Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":105,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:08.658955237Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -20"]},{"seq":106,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:14.582139774Z","text":"The `simp only` expanded the real/imaginary parts of casts of reals to complex. The `hre` pattern `Int.fract z.re + Int.floor z.re` doesn't appear because `simp` turned `(↑(Int.fract z.re)).re` into something different. Let me use a different approach — just `omega` after `push_cast`:"},{"seq":107,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:14.582665422Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":108,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:23.413724481Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -15"]},{"seq":109,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:33.309734807Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | tail -15"]},{"seq":110,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:38.662359823Z","text":"The `ring` fails because `push_cast` leaves some goals. The issue is that the goal after `simp only` + `push_cast` has casts of real values to complex, then taking `.re`. Let me try a different approach — avoid `Complex.ext_iff` and use `Complex.ext` directly:"},{"seq":111,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:38.662984883Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":112,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:48.249417721Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -20"]},{"seq":113,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:54.027572042Z","text":"The issue: after `push_cast`, the terms `(↑(Int.fract z.re)).re` don't simplify to `Int.fract z.re`. The real part of a cast of a real to complex is itself. But `push_cast` doesn't know `Complex.re`. Let me add `Complex.ofReal_re` to simp:"},{"seq":114,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:42:54.028385917Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":115,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:03.068009168Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -15"]},{"seq":116,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:14.813903441Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | grep \"⊢\\|a✝\""]},{"seq":117,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:20.802482614Z","text":"The `(↑(Int.fract z.im) * I).re` doesn't simplify because `Complex.ofReal_re` simplifies `↑x.re` not `(↑x * I).re`. I need `Complex.mul_re` and `Complex.I_re = 0`. Let me add those:"},{"seq":118,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:20.803236504Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":119,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:21.074477353Z","text":"[auto-continue 3/8]"},{"seq":120,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:34.048322283Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -15"]},{"seq":121,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:43.697486398Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | grep \"a✝\\|⊢\""]},{"seq":122,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:50.104577297Z","text":"The `(↑⌊z.re⌋).re` doesn't simplify to `⌊z.re⌋`. The cast `↑⌊z.re⌋` is `ℤ → ℂ` or `ℝ → ℂ`? It's `ℤ → ℂ` (from `Int.floor z.re : ℤ`). But `Complex.ofReal_re` is for `ℝ → ℂ` casts. I need `Complex.toComplex_re` or `Int.cast` specific lemmas. Let me use `norm_num` instead:"},{"seq":123,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:50.105253303Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":124,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:43:59.455879439Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -15"]},{"seq":125,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:05.227959980Z","text":"Those lemma names don't exist. The issue is `(↑⌊z.re⌋ : ℂ).re` where `⌊z.re⌋ : ℤ`. This is the real part of casting an Int to ℂ. I need a simp lemma for that. Let me just use `norm_num` or `push_cast` to handle all casts at once:"},{"seq":126,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:05.228657009Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":127,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:11.502562393Z","text":"Actually, the problem is that `(↑⌊z.re⌋ : ℂ).re` where `⌊z.re⌋ : ℤ` needs `Complex.ofReal_intCast` or `Rat.cast` lemmas. Let me just use `norm_num` which handles all numeric coercions:"},{"seq":128,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:11.503469979Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":129,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:21.774106077Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -15"]},{"seq":130,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:28.377463456Z","text":"The `norm_num` can't take `z` as an argument (it's a variable, not a let-declaration). And the membership proof has a different issue — `Set.mem_Icc` gives `⟨a ≤ x, x ≤ b⟩` not a single value. Let me restructure:"},{"seq":131,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:28.378089048Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93A03/../../../apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":132,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:33.216682134Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":133,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:46.016211822Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -20"]},{"seq":134,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:50.725418502Z","text":"The `(↑⌊z.re⌋ : ℂ).re` still doesn't simplify. The issue is that `↑⌊z.re⌋ : ℤ → ℂ` is `Int.cast`, and `Complex.re (Int.cast n)` is... Let me check:"},{"seq":135,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:50.731818701Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && grep -rn \"ofReal_intCast\\|intCast_re\\|Int.cast.*re\\b\\|toComplex.*intCast\" .lake/packages/m"]},{"seq":136,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:56.960036530Z","text":"`Complex.ofReal_intCast : ↑↑n = ↑(n : ℝ)`. So `(↑(n : ℤ) : ℂ) = Complex.ofReal (↑n : ℝ)`. And then `Complex.ofReal_re : (↑(x : ℝ) : ℂ).re = x`. So `(↑⌊z.re⌋ : ℂ).re = ↑⌊z.re⌋ : ℝ`. But `linarith` needs to see through this. Let me add `Complex.ofReal_intCast` to the simp set:"},{"seq":137,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:44:56.960748930Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":138,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:45:06.998221373Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -15"]},{"seq":139,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:45:16.213706836Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | grep \"a✝\\|⊢\""]},{"seq":140,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:45:22.572154168Z","text":"Still `(↑⌊z.re⌋).re`. The `Complex.ofReal_intCast` converts `↑(↑n : ℤ) = ↑(↑n : ℝ)` but the floor `⌊z.re⌋ : ℤ` gets cast directly to ℂ. Maybe the issue is that `Int.floor` returns `ℤ` and `↑⌊z.re⌋ : ℂ` is `Int.cast` not `ofReal ∘ Int.cast`. Let me try adding `Int.cast_id` or using `push_cast` before `simp`:\n\nActually, the simplest fix: just use `omega` instead of `linarith` after a `push_cast`:"},{"seq":141,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:45:22.572832262Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":142,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:45:31.071800464Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -15"]},{"seq":143,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:45:37.962549252Z","text":"`omega` can't see through `(↑⌊z.re⌋).re` either. The fundamental issue: `Complex.re` of a cast from ℤ to ℂ is not automatically simplified. Let me just use `ring` after manually providing the simplification:"},{"seq":144,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:45:37.963125743Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":145,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:45:50.057355752Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -15"]},{"seq":146,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:01.717101890Z","text":"The `ext` still doesn't work on ℂ and `linear_combination` syntax is wrong. Given the time constraints, let me commit the current partial. The proof is very close — only the complex number equality proof is blocking:"},{"seq":147,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:01.717604737Z","tools":["write_file"],"previews":["write_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":148,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:11.478597938Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -10"]},{"seq":149,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:20.434314028Z","text":"The `Set.mem_Icc` expands to `⟨a ≤ x, x ≤ b⟩` which is `And`. So the `exact` should give 4 separate arguments matching `⟨0 ≤ x, x ≤ 1, 0 ≤ y, y ≤ 1⟩`. The issue is the `simp only [Set.mem_Icc]` expands to `0 ≤ Int.fract z.re ∧ Int.fract z.re ≤ 1 ∧ 0 ≤ Int.fract z.im ∧ Int.fract z.im ≤ 1` which is right-associated `And`. Let me use `And.intro` explicitly:"},{"seq":150,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:20.444609051Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":151,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:30.404930949Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -10"]},{"seq":152,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:37.920839725Z","text":"1 sorry remaining (the complex number equality). Let me commit this state:"},{"seq":153,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:37.964440003Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && git add problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean problems/a93J05/status.json && git commit -m \"a93J0"]},{"seq":154,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:45.088835289Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe && python3 /home/joe/code/futon3c/scripts/agency_send.py --from zai-5 --to ground-control --kind bell <<'BE"]},{"seq":155,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:45.258551330Z","text":"[auto-continue 4/8]"},{"seq":156,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:53.315517195Z","text":"Let me try to close the final sorry — the complex number equality. The key insight: use `Complex.ext` and handle the `.re`/`.im` parts with explicit `show` + `ring`:"},{"seq":157,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:46:53.316183708Z","tools":["edit_file"],"previews":["edit_file /home/joe/code/apm-lean/problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean"]},{"seq":158,"type":"tool_use","at":"2026-07-26T20:47:07.195505992Z","tools":["run_shell"],"previews":["run_shell cd /home/joe/code/apm-lean && lake env lean problems/a93J05/lean/Main.lean 2>&1 | head -20"]},{"seq":159,"type":"text","at":"2026-07-26T20:47:15.958996303Z","text":"The `simp` expanded the `mul_re` but left `(↑⌊z.im⌋).re` and `(↑⌊z.im⌋).im` unsimplified. The `(↑⌊z.im⌋ * I : ℂ).re` pattern doesn't match because `simp` already expanded `Complex.mul_re`. Let me simplify the `.r